[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
mcp-grafana runs as the grafana user and group, created by www/grafana.

To run it as a service:

  1. Set GRAFANA_URL, and optionally tokens, in the environment file the
     package created from the sample (mode 0600):
       %%PREFIX%%/etc/mcp_grafana.env

  2. Enable it in /etc/rc.conf, passing any mcp-grafana options in
     mcp_grafana_flags:
       mcp_grafana_enable="YES"
       mcp_grafana_flags="--address 0.0.0.0:8443 --allowed-hosts mcp.example.com:8443"

  3. service mcp_grafana start

Without --address the server listens on localhost:8000. Once --allowed-hosts is
given, only those Host names are accepted. For HTTPS add --server.tls-cert-file
and --server.tls-key-file; the key must be readable by the grafana user.
Output goes to syslog.
EOM
}
]
